+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"329c8f1acf2ef152da0f24369c8b4f54c68aa2b5451c9011908514612f66f04f","event_uuid":"4b2b00e2-410f-4820-af28-36bfd0d9b21f","position":{"commit_sha":"12f499457a91a5f00a2d97edf4b09a2c8b7ba86d","position":"1794252775130044001-4b2b00e2-410f-4820-af28-36bfd0d9b21f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3334 patchset 1, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved; merged on main as 872e7f6c3fd092b6dd87225a07bd2633f2e5b3cb. Local: make verify exit 0 (20847 passed default tier, 202 passed integration tier); structural test observed failing on the unfixed tree first. In CI (run 42679537523) the pwsh test test_setup_uv_download_survives_two_504s executed (about 21 s on py3.11/3.12/3.13 ubuntu cells) and passed. Dispatch proof run on main: 42684304178 (in progress).","timestamp":1794252775130044001}],"created_at":1794248672470420001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c9c2c186-e9b4-496f-b0b4-313c530be0a6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4245-9f90-9d32-44c0"},{"link_uuid":"fd938ab2-7631-46d3-8364-03787b7a368d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4cac-4369-cc01-4d7d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe local `.github/actions/setup-uv` composite action downloads the uv release with a single anonymous `Invoke-WebRequest` against `https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/<version>/<asset>` and has no retry. When GitHub's release-download edge returns a transient 5xx, the step fails at once and every job that installs uv goes red before it tests anything. Every workflow uses this action, including the per-change `Verified` pipeline.\n\nObserved on the scheduled `Live External Integration` run 42572022074 (2026-11-08 22:16 PST, head `0f409b946e4`): 5 of the 9 setup-uv invocations failed within the same minute with `504 Gateway Time-out The server didn't respond in time.` at the `Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -OutFile $archive` line (langfuse, jira DC smoke, Pandoc ubuntu, Pandoc macos, live bedrock). In the same minute, 4 other jobs downloaded the identical uv 0.13.6 asset successfully (the openai arm logged `Successfully installed uv 0.13.6 from uv-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz`, 1 second before the langfuse job's 504 on the same asset). GitHub's status feed records the incident \"Increased timeouts due to surge in anonymous users\" on 2026-11-09 (\"high rates of 504 errors for anonymous requests\"; \"Logged-in users and authenticated requests are unaffected\"), plus a related unauthenticated-timeout incident on 2026-11-08. The asset downloads with HTTP 200 now.\n\nThe uv version and checksums are not the cause: the 2026-11-02 scheduled run (head `c43d9336262`) already installed uv 0.13.6 through this action and every setup-uv step passed. Change 3291 (`e0ab18822c6`) changed how the action obtains the version string but not the URL, the asset, or the download line that failed.\n\nThe bedrock arm's second failure, `Summarize LLM token usage` (`No module named 'rebar'`), is a downstream effect of the same failure: that step runs under `if: always()` and the package was never installed because setup-uv failed.\n\nFound while verifying `unkempt-amaranth-archerfish`.\n\n## Approach\n\nGive the download a bounded retry using PowerShell's built-in `Invoke-WebRequest -MaximumRetryCount 5 -RetryIntervalSec 10`. PowerShell 7 retries the request when it receives a status from 400 to 599 (or 304), waits the interval between attempts, and writes `-OutFile` only for the successful response; the SHA-256 check that follows is unchanged, so a retried download is verified exactly as before. The worst case adds 50 seconds before a persistent failure surfaces, and a persistent error (for example a 404 for a wrong version) still fails the step with the final response.\n\nWhy this fits: the failure is a short-lived upstream 5xx on some requests (4 of 9 succeeded in the same minute), which a bounded retry absorbs. It adds no input, env var, config key, or feature flag, and needs no token. Sending the workflow token was considered and rejected: it would add an env var to the step, and a public report of the same incident shows authenticated `releases/download` requests still returning 504.\n\nPortability: the retry lives in the action's own PowerShell command, so it applies on every runner OS the action supports and adds no CI-only trigger.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml`: add `-MaximumRetryCount 5 -RetryIntervalSec 10` to the `Invoke-WebRequest` download line, with a one-line comment naming this failure.\n- `tests/unit/test_setup_uv_download_retry.py` (new): regression tests for the download command.\n\n## Testing\n\nWritten first and run against the unfixed tree to confirm they fail:\n- Happy path (structure): `test_setup_uv_download_retries_transient_failures` loads `action.yml` with `yaml.safe_load`, finds the step whose `run` script contains `Invoke-WebRequest`, and asserts the call carries `-MaximumRetryCount` of at least 3 and a `-RetryIntervalSec`. On `origin/main` it fails because the call has neither.\n- Behaviour, failure-then-success: `test_setup_uv_download_survives_two_504s` starts a local `http.server` on 127.0.0.1 that answers the first 2 requests with 504 and the third with a fixed payload, extracts the action's `Invoke-WebRequest` line verbatim, runs it under `pwsh` with `$url` pointing at the local server, and asserts the output file equals the payload and the server saw 3 requests. Skipped when `pwsh` is not on PATH (GitHub's ubuntu, macOS and Windows runners ship it, so CI runs it).\n- Edge, persistent failure: `test_setup_uv_download_fails_on_persistent_504` uses a server that always answers 504 with the retry interval overridden to 1 second in the extracted line, and asserts `pwsh` exits non-zero and no output file is written. Skipped without `pwsh`.\n- The existing `tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py` and `python scripts/check_uv_pin.py` confirm the action still passes the uv pin gate.\n\nNo autouse fixtures and no new shared test helpers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The `Invoke-WebRequest` download in `.github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml` carries `-MaximumRetryCount 5 -RetryIntervalSec 10`; verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_setup_uv_download_retry.py` passing, after the structural test was observed failing on the unfixed tree.\n- [ ] The uv pin gate accepts the tree: `python scripts/check_uv_pin.py` exits 0 and `pytest tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py` passes.\n- [ ] `make lint` (with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on `PATH`) exits 0.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The change lands through Gerrit at `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`; the change number and merged SHA are recorded as a ticket comment.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A `workflow_dispatch` run of `Live External Integration` on `main` after the merge shows every setup-uv step succeeding; the run id and per-job setup-uv outcomes are recorded as a ticket comment.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":".github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml","reason":"add a bounded retry to the uv release download"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_setup_uv_download_retry.py","reason":"new regression tests for the download command"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4cac-4369-cc01-4d7d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"085638b2-2b81-4703-a1b9-cc3090531b97","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_id":"6bb6-8c88-20ad-46a9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"setup-uv download fails the job on a transient GitHub release 504 (no retry)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2706ca40-18c2-4b9d-adf7-a8a122459ec2","c9c2c186-e9b4-496f-b0b4-313c530be0a6","0ac6def5-34a2-4ef9-967a-3f20830f44b3","8702bd56-0c25-441a-8f60-1e8cc1723bfa","085638b2-2b81-4703-a1b9-cc3090531b97","67429d86-b04b-4f19-a712-9689872f0186","fd938ab2-7631-46d3-8364-03787b7a368d","4b2b00e2-410f-4820-af28-36bfd0d9b21f"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794252775130044002,"uuid":"c93e5f03-6ffc-4fbb-8b31-a83dfca8cb8a"}